{"id":"diagram-013ab5ed-10f3-429b-8504-fd27b4193510","revision":0,"diagramId":"diagram-0aea00c9-cd9c-4c3a-a399-1380bce69a31","revisionId":"diagram-revision-fbf35139-9787-49a2-8b16-bebb7fa7165b","content":{"revisionId":"diagram-013ab5ed-10f3-429b-8504-fd27b4193510:0","ascii":"T2b - Recording and history boundaries\n|-- Peripheral to T2a / process / fine\n|-- Scope: incoming diffs, recording modes and marks\n\n|-- Store history interceptor receives (entry, source)\n|   |-- source != user -> do not record\n|   `-- source == user -> inspect recorder state\n|       |-- Recording\n|       |   |-- Apply changes to pendingDiff\n|       |   `-- Clear redo stack\n|       |-- RecordingPreserveRedoStack\n|       |   `-- Apply changes; retain redo stack\n|       `-- Paused -> do not record\n\n|-- editor.run(fn, {history})\n|   |-- record / record-preserveRedoStack / ignore\n|   |-- Synchronous batch under a reactive transaction\n|   |-- Restore previous mode when the call finishes\n|   `-- A nested batch cannot override an existing pause\n\n|-- markHistoryStoppingPoint() -> history._mark()\n|   |-- Flush nonempty pendingDiff onto undo stack\n|   `-- Push stop entry with mark id\n\n|-- squashToMark(markId)\n|   `-- Merge stacked diffs since that mark\n\n`-- Policies to keep separate\n    |-- Batching is not automatic rollback on an exception\n    |-- Marks define stopping points across many writes\n    |-- Scope is not the history recording policy\n    `-- API / network origin alone does not make a write remote","asciiSha256":"d958bad11f00ebd6fe3377d4b43da3fa27c7cec346d67924fa7c559caec33135","structure":{"kind":"tree","parserVersion":"ascii-tree-2","rootIds":["diagram-013ab5ed-10f3-429b-8504-fd27b4193510:0:d958bad11f00ebd6fe3377d4b43da3fa27c7cec346d67924fa7c559caec33135:line-1"],"nodes":{"diagram-013ab5ed-10f3-429b-8504-fd27b4193510:0:d958bad11f00ebd6fe3377d4b43da3fa27c7cec346d67924fa7c559caec33135:line-1":{"id":"diagram-013ab5ed-10f3-429b-8504-fd27b4193510:0:d958bad11f00ebd6fe33